{"path":"string/basic_string_view/data","title":"std::basic_string_view<CharT,Traits>::data","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_string_view&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>data","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/data","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a pointer to the underlying character array. The pointer is such that the range [data(), data() + size()) is valid and the values in it correspond to the values of the view.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> const_pointer data<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a pointer to the underlying character array. The pointer is such that the range <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">data<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">data<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> size<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code><code>)</code></span> is valid and the values in it correspond to the values of the view.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A pointer to the underlying character array.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Unlike <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/data\">std::basic_string::data()</a></span> and string literals, <code>std::basic_string_view::data()</code> returns a pointer to a buffer that is not necessarily null-terminated, for example a substring view (e.g. from <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/remove_suffix\"><code>remove_suffix</code></a>). Therefore, it is typically a mistake to pass <code>data()</code> to a routine that takes just a <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> CharT<span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code> and expects a null-terminated string.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstring&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cwchar&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string_view&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1258\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wstring_view</span></span></a> wcstr_v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> L<span class=\"st0\">\"xyzzy\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/wide/wcslen\"><span class=\"kw1220\">std::<span class=\"me2\">wcslen</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>wcstr_v.<span class=\"me1\">data</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// OK: the underlying character array is null-terminated</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> array<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'B'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'a'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'r'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> array_v<span class=\"br0\">(</span>array, sizeof array<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// std::cout &lt;&lt; std::strlen(array_v.data()) &lt;&lt; '\\n';</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// error: the underlying character array is not null-terminated</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> str<span class=\"br0\">(</span>array_v.<span class=\"me1\">data</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, array_v.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// OK</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strlen\"><span class=\"kw1153\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strlen</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str.<span class=\"me1\">data</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// OK: the underlying character array of a std::string is always null-terminated</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>5\n3</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/front\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>front</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  accesses the first character <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/back\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>back</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  accesses the last character <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string/data\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>data</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a pointer to the first character of a string <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::basic_string&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/basic_string_view","title":"std::basic_string_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_string_view<CharT,Traits>::data","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++17. Returns a pointer to the underlying character array."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A pointer to the underlying character array."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Unlike std::basic_string::data() and string literals, std::basic_string_view::data() returns a pointer to a buffer that is not necessarily null-terminated…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"front","note":"accesses the first character"},{"label":"back","note":"accesses the last character"},{"label":"data","note":"returns a pointer to the first character of a string"}]}]},"standards":["C++17"],"wordCount":218,"codeBlockCount":2}
